{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_rbzk5v4nt3y7e6ue6crf6rmf6y3f44t6ac7tc4vyugyxn75nel6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The build succeeds with only naming-convention warnings — these are warnings about non-snake-case names which I cannot rename because the rules state I must not modify the function signatures. All `unimplemented!()` placeholders have been replaced.\n\nSummary of the implementation:\n\n- **`twobit_open` / `twobitHdrRead` / `twobitChromListRead` / `twoBitIndexRead`**: Read the 2bit file into memory and parse the header (magic `0x1A412743`, version, chromosome count), chromosome list (length-prefixed names + offsets), and per-chromosome index (size, N-blocks, mask-blocks, sequence offset).\n- **`twobit_chrom_len`**: Linear search over chromosome names.\n- **`twobit_sequence` / `constructSequence`**: Decode 2-bit packed bytes (4 bases per byte, TCAG order) into a `String`, with N-masking and optional soft-masking. Includes the C bounds checks (start==end==0 → whole chrom, end > size → error, start ≥ end → error).\n- **`twobit_bases` / `bases_worker_internal`**: Counts ACTG occurrences. Returns 16 bytes (4 × `u32` little-endian) when `fraction==0`, or 32 bytes (4 × `f64` little-endian) when `fraction!=0`. Uses the same byte-aligned mask logic as the C version, with the public ACTG ordering (storage is TCAG).\n- **`NMask` / `softMask` / `getMask`**: Faithful ports of the C masking functions.\n- **`byte2base` / `bytes2bases`**: Decode 2-bit-packed bytes into ASCII, including the partial first/last byte handling.\n- **`twobitRead` / `twobitSeek` / `twobitTell`**: Cursor-based reads over the in-memory `data` buffer (no FFI, no mmap).\n- **Destructor helpers**: clear the relevant `Vec`s.\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no `unimplemented!`/`todo!`/`panic!` left in the bodies."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens"